# Frontend Components

- Keep components cleanly segregated — one component owns one concern (a page, or one self-contained piece of UI). Don't let unrelated logic accumulate in a component just because it's convenient to bolt on.
- Target **~200 lines per component**. Going over is fine when a component genuinely needs it — treat 200 as the point where you ask "should this split?", not a hard limit to engineer around.
- Split by responsibility, not just to hit a line count:
  - Extract a subcomponent when a piece of JSX has its own clear purpose.
  - Extract a hook when logic (data fetching, derived state) is reusable, or is cluttering the component body.

## Folder structure — `src/components/`

Every shared component is a folder, named for the component, holding only the files it needs:

```
src/components/Button/
  Button.tsx           # renders — JSX and DOM-facing logic only
  Button.helper.ts      # non-DOM logic the component needs before it renders
  Button.module.scss    # only if Tailwind's utility classes can't express the style
  Button.test.tsx       # only once a test is actually written
```

- **`Button.tsx`** renders. Data should already be in the shape it needs by the time it reaches JSX.
- **`Button.helper.ts`** holds logic that never touches the DOM — sorting, filtering, reshaping data, computing a derived value. If a function doesn't reference JSX or the DOM, it belongs here, not inline in the component.
- **`Button.module.scss`** uses CSS Modules — Vite scopes its class names to this file automatically, so they can't collide with another component's styles (`sass` is already a dev dependency so this resolves out of the box). This is the exception, not the default: reach for it only when Tailwind's utilities genuinely can't express the style.
- **`Button.test.tsx`** is co-located, not in a separate `__tests__/` tree.

This convention is for `src/components/` specifically. `src/pages/` stays flat (`src/pages/LeaderboardPage.tsx`) — pages are route-level containers, not reusable components.

## Shared utilities — `src/utils/`

Logic used by only one component lives in that component's `*.helper.ts`. Once a second component needs the same logic, promote it to a flat file in `src/utils/` (e.g. `src/utils/formatDate.ts`) so both import it from one place instead of duplicating it.
